course: dictionary
lesson: 5623
title: Likewise: the same, also, or the same to you
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Likewise is a small word with a few jobs. Its first job is to mean in the same way. In the sentence «Go and do likewise», you are told to act the same way as the example you have just seen. The word asks you to copy.
explain: Its second job is to add a similar point, meaning also or as well. Look for it when one idea is followed by another idea that matches it. Ask yourself: is the second idea the same kind of thing as the first? If yes, likewise probably means also.
explain: Its third job happens in speech. When someone says «Nice to meet you», a short reply of «Likewise» is informal and means the same to you, or I feel the same. Swap in «the same to you» and see if it still makes sense. If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Likewise means in the same way, as in «Go and do likewise».
fact: Likewise can mean also or as well, when you add a similar point.
fact: As a short reply, «Likewise» means the same to you, or I feel the same. This is informal, so use it with friends and people you know well.
fact: Likewise is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done or links one idea to another.
fact: A good check is to swap in «also», «in the same way» or «the same to you» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Watch me carefully and do likewise.» What does likewise mean here? | Not at all | *In the same way | Very quickly | In a different way
exercise: Ben says, «I like football, and likewise I like swimming.» What does likewise add? | A different, opposite point | A question | *Also, a similar point
exercise: Your friend says, «Nice to meet you.» You reply, «Likewise.» What do you mean? | Goodbye forever | I do not agree with you | I am leaving now | *The same to you, I feel the same
test: «Go and do likewise.» Which words are the best swap for likewise here? | *In the same way | Never | Backwards | Quietly and slowly
test: Mia says, «I play the piano, and likewise my brother does.» What does likewise tell you about the brother? | Mia stopped playing | *The brother plays too, as well as Mia | The brother never plays | The brother plays a different instrument
exam: Tom says, «Good luck in the race!» You reply, «Likewise.» What have you said? | *Good luck to you too | I want you to win too | Thank you for the luck | Goodbye, see you later
